WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.150
From the 1970s, much manufacturing moved
from high-income countries to emerging

2
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.170
economies, drawn by lower costs.

3
00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:14.230
One study found that in 2006, 36 per cent
of China's human-made sulphur dioxide

4
00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.330
was linked to producing goods for export.

5
00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:21.030
So was 27 per cent of its nitrogen oxides.

6
00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:22.750
Whose pollution is it?

7
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.930
China's, because it was emitted there?

8
00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:27.790
Or nobody's, because trade is neutral?

9
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.970
In this mission, you'll trace
the global shift of industry,

10
00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:34.470
and test the pollution haven hypothesis.

11
00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:36.990
Then you'll follow export
pollution across the Pacific,

12
00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.670
and soy into the Amazon.

13
00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:44.530
Your mission: decide whose pollution it
is when Chinese factories make goods for

14
00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:45.320
export.
